WEBVTT

00:00:00.162 --> 00:00:02.459
What actually pops when you crack your
knuckles?

00:00:02.812 --> 00:00:03.869
Not your bones.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.200
Your joints sit in a capsule of fluid.

00:00:06.493 --> 00:00:10.817
Pull the joint apart, the pressure drops,
and a gas cavity snaps open.

00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:15.407
In 2015, scientists filmed it inside an
MRI.

00:00:15.636 --> 00:00:17.811
The pop happened as the bubble formed.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:22.655
A 2018 model says a partial collapse could
still make the sound.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.124
The debate isn't over.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:25.605
And arthritis?

00:00:25.842 --> 00:00:29.097
A study of 215 people found no link.

00:00:29.452 --> 00:00:30.654
So it's just a bubble.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.021
Do you crack yours?
